WHAT THIS FILE DOES AND DOES NOT DO

It does not prevent copying, and nobody should treat it as a technical
control. A web application serves its own markup, styles and client-side code
to every visitor by necessity; anyone can read them. This file does not change
that and is not intended to.

What it does is remove the ambiguity. A repository with no licence invites the
argument that its author did not mind. This one says plainly that permission
was never given, which is what matters if the question is ever put to anyone
other than a developer.

